= The Republic Builds Homes

SLD's programme called for a National Housebuilding Programme. Its mayors now
want land, financing and public contractors aligned around homes for long-term
rent rather than another credit subsidy that follows prices upward.

- @sld_homes_national
- @sld_homes_municipal
- @sld_homes_refuse

@sld_homes_national
title: Create a national public housebuilder
subtitle: Cost: 3 budget capacity. Supply and security rise sharply; fiscal and coalition pressure follow.
choose-if: budget >= 3
unavailable-subtitle: Capitalising the national housebuilder needs three budget points.
on-arrival: budget -= 3; fiscal_stress += 3; public_debt += 2; barons_strength += 5; barons_dissent -= 9; household_security += 8; government_delivery += 5; government_goal_housing = 1; public_sector_support += 5; workers_support += 3; economic_growth += 0.4; unemployment -= 0.3; market_liberal_dissent += 6; ko_relation -= 4; p2050_relation -= 3; government_coalition_dissent += 4; news_headline = "Government creates a national public housebuilder"

The company builds on public land and keeps the homes in a permanent rental
stock. Delivery is slower than a rebate and cannot be capitalised into a private sale.

- #poland_card_finish

