card-image: img/poland/cards/group-labour.webp

= Six Hours Is a Working Day

PPS argues that enforcing the eight-hour day is only the precondition. Its
programme then cuts normal work to at least six hours a day with no loss of pay.
Employers calculate shifts; workers calculate recovered life.

- @pps_six_hour_law
- @pps_six_hour_sector
- @pps_six_hour_refuse

@pps_six_hour_law
title: Legislate a thirty-hour week without loss of pay
subtitle: A historic labour victory; costs, staffing and coalition conflict hit immediately.
on-arrival: pps_strength += 6; pps_dissent -= 11; labor_strength += 3; workers_support += 8; union_trust += 7; labor_credibility += 6; government_goal_labor = 1; unemployment -= 0.4; economic_growth -= 0.5; inflation += 0.4; public_sector_support += 4; market_liberal_dissent += 10; ko_relation -= 8; p2050_relation -= 7; psl_relation -= 5; government_coalition_dissent += 9; early_election_risk += 4; news_headline = "Government legislates a six-hour working day without loss of pay"

The legal week falls to thirty hours. Productivity agreements may rearrange
the clock, but may not return the surrendered hours through unpaid overtime.

- #poland_card_finish

@pps_six_hour_sector
title: Begin with public services and high-intensity sectors
subtitle: Cost: 2 budget capacity. Test staffing and productivity under collective agreements.
choose-if: budget >= 2
unavailable-subtitle: Replacement staffing and sectoral bargaining need two budget points.
on-arrival: budget -= 2; pps_strength += 3; pps_dissent -= 6; labor_strength += 2; workers_support += 5; union_trust += 5; labor_credibility += 4; government_goal_labor = 1; public_sector_support += 6; unemployment -= 0.2; market_liberal_dissent += 5; ko_relation -= 3; government_coalition_dissent += 4; news_headline = "Six-hour days begin under public and sectoral agreements"

Care, hazardous work and selected public services go first. The pilots are
collective agreements with an expansion date, not productivity seminars.

- #poland_card_finish

@pps_six_hour_refuse
title: Enforce the existing eight-hour day
subtitle: Free. Win a practical labour reform; PPS says the promised frontier has become the old minimum.
on-arrival: poland_pps_six_hour_timer = 8; pps_dissent += 11; pps_strength -= 2; labor_credibility += 2; union_trust += 1; workers_support += 2; economic_growth += 0.1; market_liberal_dissent -= 3; ko_relation += 3; news_headline = "Cabinet enforces the eight-hour day but rejects PPS's six-hour law"

Unpaid overtime finally draws real penalties. The working day becomes honest
and remains eight hours long.

- #poland_card_finish


