= The Last Night of Homelessness

PPS's housing chapter makes an absolute promise: end homelessness by providing
a public dwelling to every person who needs one. Services follow the home rather
than making perfect stability a condition for receiving it.

- @pps_housing_guarantee
- @pps_housing_first_cities
- @pps_housing_refuse

@pps_housing_guarantee
title: Establish a national housing-first guarantee
subtitle: Cost: 3 budget capacity. Security and trust rise sharply; municipalities must acquire homes immediately.
choose-if: budget >= 3
unavailable-subtitle: The national acquisition and support fund needs three budget points.
on-arrival: budget -= 3; fiscal_stress += 2; pps_strength += 5; pps_dissent -= 10; household_security += 10; government_goal_housing = 1; public_trust += 6; institutional_trust += 4; local_network += 4; public_sector_support += 4; universal_solidarity += 5; government_delivery += 5; psl_relation -= 2; government_coalition_dissent += 3; news_headline = "Government guarantees a public home before support conditions"

Municipalities acquire units, the state covers support and nobody must prove
housing readiness while unhoused. The promise creates a waiting list the law
requires government to eliminate.

- #poland_card_finish

@pps_housing_first_cities
