= Fibre Is a Public Right

PPS calls access to information a human right and promises fibre through a
public provider or consumer cooperatives. Commercial networks may carry the
traffic; they may not decide which address is worth connecting.

- @pps_fibre_provider
- @pps_fibre_coops
- @pps_fibre_refuse

@pps_fibre_provider
title: Create a public universal-service provider
subtitle: Cost: 3 budget capacity. Rural access and state capacity rise; private providers contest the network.
choose-if: budget >= 3
unavailable-subtitle: Capitalising a universal fibre provider needs three budget points.
