= Eight Reactors, Twelve Gigawatts

Razem's industrial programme specifies at least eight large nuclear blocks with
twelve gigawatts of capacity, backed by grid modernisation and domestic skills.
The cabinet must decide whether the number is a national plan or an opposition
leaflet written before the procurement files arrived.

- @razem_reactors_eight
- @razem_reactors_sequence
- @razem_reactors_refuse

@razem_reactors_eight
title: Finance the full eight-block public programme
subtitle: Cost: 4 budget capacity. Energy sovereignty and industrial planning surge; debt and delivery risk follow.
choose-if: budget >= 4
unavailable-subtitle: The first capital tranche of the full programme needs four budget points.
on-arrival: budget -= 4; fiscal_stress += 4; public_debt += 3; razem_strength += 6; razem_dissent -= 10; energy_security += 10; climate_state_capacity += 8; administrative_capacity += 5; public_sector_support += 6; workers_support += 5; economic_growth += 0.7; unemployment -= 0.4; government_delivery += 4; market_liberal_dissent += 6; ko_relation -= 3; government_coalition_dissent += 5; news_headline = "Government commits to eight public nuclear blocks and twelve gigawatts"

A single state programme orders reactors, grids, training and domestic supply
chains as one sequence. The horizon is long enough to outlive this cabinet and
the liabilities arrive early enough to belong to it.

- #poland_card_finish

@razem_reactors_sequence
title: Authorise four blocks with an option for four more
subtitle: Cost: 3 budget capacity. Preserve the industrial direction while making later blocks earn approval.
choose-if: budget >= 3
unavailable-subtitle: The first four-block programme needs three budget points.
