= Public Money, Public Code

Razem wants public institutions off permanent rent to foreign technology firms.
Its rule is simple: software created with public money is open by default, and
the state operates public data infrastructure rather than scattering sensitive
systems across proprietary clouds.

- @razem_code_sovereign
- @razem_code_open_default
- @razem_code_refuse

@razem_code_sovereign
title: Build a public cloud and require open code by default
subtitle: Cost: 3 budget capacity. Capacity and sovereignty rise; migration costs and vendors hit the cabinet at once.
choose-if: budget >= 3
unavailable-subtitle: Public infrastructure and migration teams need three budget points.
on-arrival: budget -= 3; fiscal_stress += 2; razem_strength += 5; razem_dissent -= 9; administrative_capacity += 8; institutional_trust += 5; media_capacity += 4; public_sector_support += 5; movement_autonomy += 4; economic_growth += 0.4; government_delivery += 4; public_trust += 4; market_liberal_dissent += 4; ko_relation -= 2; government_coalition_dissent += 3; news_headline = "Government builds a sovereign public cloud and opens taxpayer-funded code"

Agencies migrate to a shared public platform and publish reusable source code
unless a security exception is documented. Procurement begins buying capability
instead of another locked door.

- #poland_card_finish

@razem_code_open_default
title: Open taxpayer-funded software before building a public cloud
subtitle: Cost: 1 budget capacity. The rule changes procurement quickly while infrastructure remains mixed.
choose-if: budget >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Auditing licences and establishing the public repository need one budget point.
on-arrival: budget -= 1; razem_strength += 3; razem_dissent -= 5; administrative_capacity += 5; institutional_trust += 4; media_capacity += 3; public_trust += 4; economic_growth += 0.2; market_liberal_dissent += 2; p2050_relation += 1; government_delivery += 2; news_headline = "Taxpayer-funded government software becomes open by default"

New contracts must deliver source code the public can inspect and reuse. Data
may still sit on commercial infrastructure, but the state can leave a supplier
without leaving its own software behind.

- #poland_card_finish

@razem_code_refuse
title: Negotiate stronger terms with existing suppliers
subtitle: Free. Avoid a costly migration; Razem says better rent is still rent.
on-arrival: poland_razem_public_code_timer = 7; razem_dissent += 8; razem_strength -= 1; administrative_capacity += 1; institutional_trust -= 1; movement_autonomy -= 2; market_liberal_dissent -= 2; ko_relation += 2; government_coalition_dissent -= 1; news_headline = "Cabinet keeps proprietary systems under revised technology contracts"

New clauses improve portability and security audits. The platforms, licences
and strategic dependency remain private.

- #poland_card_finish


