= Choose Your Waiting Room

Razem links two demands: public health spending of at least eight percent of GDP,
and a choice for doctors between public employment and simultaneous private
practice. The party calls it an end to paid shortcuts through public queues;
medical organisations call it an ultimatum to an already thin workforce.

- @razem_health_separate
- @razem_health_eight_percent
- @razem_health_refuse

@razem_health_separate
title: Fund eight percent and require a choice of practice
subtitle: Cost: 4 budget capacity. Public capacity and equality surge; staffing and coalition conflict peak immediately.
choose-if: budget >= 4
unavailable-subtitle: The funding path and public-sector retention package need four budget points.
on-arrival: budget -= 4; fiscal_stress += 4; public_debt += 2; razem_strength += 6; razem_dissent -= 10; health_capacity += 10; government_goal_health = 1; public_sector_support += 8; workers_support += 5; women_support += 4; household_security += 6; universal_solidarity += 5; government_delivery += 5; public_trust += 4; market_liberal_dissent += 8; ko_relation -= 6; p2050_relation -= 5; government_coalition_dissent += 7; early_election_risk += 2; news_headline = "Public health receives an eight-percent path and doctors must choose one practice"

Public salaries rise before the separation takes effect. A doctor may remain in
public care or leave for private practice, but may no longer sell access beside
the queue they also control.

- #poland_card_finish

